tedHypergraph-Implementations","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/Encodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/Hashable-Implementations","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/PropertyGraph-Implementations"],"generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the matrix of Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen (1993). A directed graph’s edge is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column with one source and one target, which gives the oriented incidence matrix of spectral","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L). The matrix conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged. It is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Two-bit-planes","text":"Two bit planes","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The sources and the targets are each stored as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a vertex can be on both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sides of a column. Its entry is then target − source = 0, with both bits kept.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"sources(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"targets(ofHyperedgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the stars and equality read the planes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so nothing is lost. A directed self-loop is such a column. ","type":"text"},{"code":"reversed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" swaps the planes, negating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every entry, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"transposed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" transposes each plane to give the dual. Both are O(1).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Storage is 4·n·m\/8 bytes, so the matrix suits dense or small incidence. ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sparse representation. Equality compares both planes cell for cell, with equal shape, so column","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order counts.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/Hashable-Implementations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/Hashable-Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/hashable-implementations","title":"Hashable Implementations","abstract":[],"kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/PropertyGraph":{"title":"PropertyGraph","fragments